  "content": {
    "id": "p29-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Consider the function $f(x)=x^2-4x+7$ for the domain $x\\geq2$. State the range of this function.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y\\geq3$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=x^2-4x+7\\\\f(x)&=(x-2)^2+3.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x\\geq2$, the minimum value is $f(2)=3$, and the function increases without bound. The range is $y\\geq3$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
